Step 12.3 — Understand what we just created

The important quantity is:

$$ \text{Utilization} = \frac{\text{Used Bandwidth}} {\text{Available Bandwidth}} $$

For example:

Bandwidth = 10 Mbps
Used      = 8 Mbps

Therefore:

$$ U = \frac{8}{10}=0.8=80\% $$

So:

80% → HIGH congestion

Our initial thresholds are:

Utilization	State
< 30%	LOW
30–70%	MEDIUM
> 70%	HIGH

These are prototype thresholds, not final research thresholds. Later we'll tune them experimentally.

Step 12.4 — Add dynamic routing weights

This is the important part.

Currently your NetworkX graph uses:

weight=1

for every link.

That means:

s1 ── s2 ── s4
 \          /
  s3 ──────

Both paths have equal cost.

So the controller may choose either:

s1 → s2 → s4

or:

s1 → s3 → s4

depending on discovery/order.

Now we'll make the cost depend on congestion.

