Step 12.5 — Why this matters for MedRoute

Your routing is now conceptually:

                  LOW congestion
                       ↓
s1 ───────────────→ s2 ─────→ s4
 │
 │
 └───────────────→ s3 ─────→ s4
                  ↑
            HIGH congestion

Suppose:

Path A:
s1 → s2 → s4

has:

s1-s2 = 20%
s2-s4 = 30%

and Path B:

s1 → s3 → s4

has:

s1-s3 = 80%
s3-s4 = 70%

Then:

Path A cost = 1 + 5 = 6
Path B cost = 10 + 10 = 20

NetworkX will prefer:

s1 → s2 → s4

This is the foundation for your later Braess-aware routing.

